    <p class="eyebrow">About the Project</p>
    <h2>A Third Library is Possible</h2>
    <div class="zigzag" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <p>In January 2022, The Council on Library and Information Resources (CLIR) introduced the Curated Futures Project, a collection of collaboratively produced works that respond to the theme “A Third Library is Possible.” The collection was created to serve as a provocation and guide for gallery, library, archive, and museum professionals to move beyond discussions of decolonizing memory organizations and begin taking practical steps to enact change.</p>
    <p>
      <em>(updated May 2023)</em>
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/about/">Learn More <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
